      "named_events": [],
      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a gross strengthening of prior year reserves of GBP 133.060 million in 2016, representing 23.31% of its opening gross claims outstanding. This was primarily driven by the revision of the Ogden discount rate from 2.5% to minus 0.75%, which resulted in a gross strengthening of GBP 155.750 million for long-tail motor liabilities. Prior to this Ogden impact, the syndicate had a release of GBP 22.690 million from its prior accident year claims provisions. The overall gross position deteriorated due to the Ogden change, though the net impact was reduced by reinsurance recoveries. The Ogden rate change affected motor liabilities from prior years.",
